{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1cc2ad08-77b4-4e55-a61b-07dbc06970c6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ac3b25adbbd80d97","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/hlx && cat > /tmp/hlx/p.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, os\nD=\"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260915T103412Z-bf20aced/runs/specialist/29596d2569b8440f8f7dfd64b072cc18\"\nGAP=\"inference:qwen3.8-27b-abliterated-w8a8-gdnint8:unknown_gpu:vllm:qwen3_5:qwen3_5forconditionalgeneration:0.28.0:bf16#throughput_below_target\"\nV=\"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm\"\nLOG=\"runs/baseline/51ac28ff8aed4ad59746fdb889fae7bb/benchmark_vllm_20260915_103510/server.log\"\n\nfindings=[\n {\"what\":\"RESOLVED residual question: the GDN Triton/FLA decode kernels do consume a narrowed recurrent state directly, and bf16 is a first-class fast-path dtype. qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:90 declares FUSED_GDN_STATE_DTYPES = (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16); that tuple is the gate for the fused decode/MTP paths (line 523, line 1806). bfloat16 is deliberately whitelisted alongside fp32, float16 is not. So --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 does NOT force a slow fallback on this build, and it is strictly better-supported than float16.\",\n  \"source\":V+\"/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:90,523,1806\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Removes the main unknown blocking the largest decode-side memory-traffic lever; state write traffic is ~75MB/req/step over 48 linear-attn layers at conc=64.\",\n  \"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"candidate_discovery\",\"gdn\",\"rocm\",\"mamba_cache\"]},\n {\"what\":\"The GDN recurrent-state dtype is set by the CHECKPOINT, not by a kernel requirement, and an explicit CLI flag overrides it with only a warning. Qwen3_5ForConditionalGenerationConfig.verify_and_update_config (model_executor/models/config.py:781-805) copies hf_text_config.mamba_ssm_dtype into cache_config.mamba_ssm_cache_dtype only when that field is 'auto'; when the user sets it explicitly the code logs 'Using the user-specified value' and proceeds. Nothing downstream asserts fp32.\",\n  \"source\":V+\"/model_executor/models/config.py:781-805; \"+V+\"/config/cache.py:133; \"+V+\"/model_executor/layers/mamba/mamba_utils.py:96-107\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Confirms --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype is a supported, non-crashing override on this exact architecture string.\",\n  \"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"gdn\",\"mamba_cache\",\"cli\"]},\n {\"what\":\"HALF the 29% prefill dead-time is already addressed: async scheduling is ON by default in this build and 'align' mamba_cache_mode is explicitly compat-patched. VllmConfig sets async_scheduling=True when it is None unless the model is pooling, a non-EAGLE spec method, or a non-supporting executor is used (config/vllm.py:1185-1234) - none apply here (speculative_config=None in the baseline engine dump). gpu_model_runner.py:2167 keys its hybrid-model CPU-sync race guard specifically on `use_async_scheduling and mamba_cache_mode != 'align'`, and the baseline log shows mode 'align'. A pure CPU-side prefill/decode-overlap lever is therefore already in the stack.\",\n  \"source\":V+\"/config/vllm.py:1185-1234,554-560; \"+V+\"/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py:2167; \"+LOG+\":14\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Kills a whole candidate class; remaining prefill-side levers must be GPU-kernel-side, not scheduler-side.\",\n  \"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"negative_knowledge\",\"scheduler\",\"prefill_overlap\"]},\n {\"what\":\"AITER's CDNA2 gate has NO env override, confirming target 5's negative answer: _aiter_ops.is_aiter_found_and_supported() returns get_cdna_version() > 2 gated only on IS_AITER_FOUND and current_platform.is_rocm(). VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 is set in the base env but that only adds 'should we use it' on top of 'can we' - the arch test still fails on gfx90a. So no env-only route to AITER GDN decode fast paths; that genuinely needs a source patch and is out of scope here.\",\n  \"source\":V+\"/_aiter_ops.py:134-155; \"+V+\"/envs.py:1242-1244; baseline_config.with_envs.yaml (VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER='1')\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Frees proposal slots from a dead end.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\n  \"domain_tags\":[\"negative_knowledge\",\"aiter\",\"cdna2\",\"rocm\"]},\n {\"what\":\"Three candidate levers present in this build are NOT applicable and should not be proposed again: (a) VLLM_GDN_DECODE_KERNEL=cuda - the baseline log already shows it fell back with 'torch.ops._C.fused_gdn_decode_post_conv_mtp is not built', i.e. the op is absent from this ROCm wheel, so no env value can enable it; (b) --enable-mamba-cache-stochastic-rounding - config/mamba.py:85-92 raises on any non-CUDA platform (and needs cvt.rs on sm100), and it also requires float16 not bfloat16; (c) --use-replayssm - the ReplaySSM ring buffers are keyed to the Mamba2 SSM state layout (mamba_attn.py:182 B_cache shape (ngroups, buffer_len, dstate)), not the GDN delta-rule state.\",\n  \"source\":V+\"/config/mamba.py:85-92; \"+V+\"/v1/attention/backends/mamba_attn.py:171-195; \"+LOG+\" (GDN decode kernel: triton)\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Prevents 3 wasted benchmark slots on paths that hard-error or no-op.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\n  \"domain_tags\":[\"negative_knowledge\",\"gdn\",\"mamba_cache\",\"rocm\"]},\n {\"what\":\"Decoder attention backend was selected by elimination and ROCM_ATTN then fell back to a Triton kernel, leaving exactly one untested alternative: 'Found incompatible backend(s) [TURBOQUANT] with AttentionType.DECODER. Overriding with ROCM_ATTN out of potential backends: [ROCM_ATTN, TRITON_ATTN]' (rocm.py:703), plus a runtime fallback into chunked_prefill_paged_decode. GDN runs on the Triton/FLA path (head_k_dim=128) and the decoder stream is head_dim=256, so the two are independent - a decoder-backend change cannot perturb GDN numerics.\",\n  \"source\":LOG+\": rocm.py:703, qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:163; \"+V+\"/v1/attention/backends/rocm_attn.py:193\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Zero-risk prefill-side probe of the only remaining backend.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none (same math, different kernel)\",\n  \"domain_tags\":[\"candidate_discovery\",\"attention_backend\",\"rocm\",\"prefill\"]},\n {\"what\":\"Mamba page size is bound to the state dtype by construction: 'Setting attention block size to 784 tokens to ensure that attention page size is >= mamba page size' and 'Padding mamba page size by 0.13%'. Halving the recurrent state fp32->bf16 shrinks the mamba page directly, which relaxes this 784-token block size. Capacity is not binding (KV usage peaks 38-48%, Waiting: 0), so the gain is per-step HBM traffic, not extra blocks.\",\n  \"source\":LOG+\": interface.py:911,935; \"+V+\"/config/cache.py:116-124\",\n  \"expected_impact\":\"Second-order amplification of the bf16-state proposal; explains why KV-capacity tuning is a dead end.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none (analysis)\",\n  \"domain_tags\":[\"mamba_cache\",\"page_size\",\"negative_knowledge\"]}\n]\n\nprops=[\n {\"name\":\"gdn_ssm_state_bf16\",\n  \"reason\":\"The ~75MB/req/step GDN recurrent-state read+write is the largest per-step HBM traffic source at conc=64, and it is fp32 ONLY because the checkpoint declares mamba_ssm_dtype='float32' and config.py:792 auto-adopts it when the flag is 'auto'. Passing --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 overrides that with a warning (not an error) and halves state traffic. Evidence this is a supported dtype rather than a forced fallback: FUSED_GDN_STATE_DTYPES=(float32,bfloat16) whitelists bf16 on the fused GDN decode paths, and mamba_utils._mamba_state_dtype reads the flag verbatim into STR_DTYPE_TO_TORCH_DTYPE. bfloat16 is chosen over float16 because it is the whitelisted dtype and shares fp32's exponent range, so a long OSL=1024 recurrence cannot overflow where fp16 could.\",\n  \"extra_args\":\"--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16\",\"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":False,\n  \"kb_evidence\":[\"prior: state cache is the single largest per-step HBM traffic source, flag is first-class in 0.28.0+rocm723\"],\n  \"pr_evidence\":[],\n  \"source_evidence\":[V+\"/model_executor/models/config.py:781-805\",V+\"/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:90,523,1806\",V+\"/model_executor/layers/mamba/mamba_utils.py:96-107\",V+\"/engine/arg_utils.py:1237\",LOG+\": interface.py:911 (784-token block bound to mamba page)\"]},\n {\"name\":\"gdn_ssm_bf16_plus_triton_attn\",\n  \"reason\":\"Combines the two live levers so the decoder-kernel swap is measured while its dominant cost (state traffic) is halved: if bf16 state frees meaningful memory-bandwidth, the prefill-side kernel difference is more visible in one run. Both halves are independently safe (TRITON_ATTN was already reported compatible; the bf16 override is the top candidate), and the combined variant is what Orchestrator should bench against baseline if only one extra slot is available.\",\n  \"extra_args\":\"--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 --attention-backend TRITON_ATTN\",\"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":False,\n  \"kb_evidence\":[\"prior: ROCM_ATTN selected by elimination and itself fell back to a Triton kernel\"],\n  \"pr_evidence\":[],\n  \"source_evidence\":[LOG+\": rocm.py:703 (TRITON_ATTN listed as compatible)\",V+\"/model_executor/models/config.py:781-805\"]},\n {\"name\":\"decoder_attn_triton_backend\",\n  \"reason\":\"Isolates the backend swap with zero numerical-precision change, as a clean attribution run and as a fallback if the accuracy gate rejects bf16 state. ROCM_ATTN was chosen only because TURBOQUANT was rejected for AttentionType.DECODER, and ROCM_ATTN then logged a fallback into chunked_prefill_paged_decode - i.e. the current path is not the merit-selected one. Prefill windows are ~29% of wall clock with near-total prefill/decode serialization, so prefill kernel cost is worth as much as decode-speed work. Decoder head_dim=256 is inside ROCM_ATTN's supported list but is the awkward size for the AITER fmha_v3 ASM path, which platform law 11 rules out here.\",\n  \"extra_args\":\"--attention-backend TRITON_ATTN\",\"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":False,\n  \"kb_evidence\":[\"prior: backend selected by elimination, not merit; accuracy_risk none\"],\n  \"pr_evidence\":[],\n  \"source_evidence\":[LOG+\": rocm.py:703, chunked_prefill_paged_decode.py:463\",V+\"/v1/attention/backends/rocm_attn.py:193\"]}\n]\n\npayload={\"intent_type\":\"specialist_done\",\"payload\":{\n \"confidence\":0.62,\"domain\":\"candidate_discovery_specialist\",\"empty\":False,\"gap_canonical_id\":GAP,\n \"new_findings\":findings,\"proposal_set\":props,\n \"residual_questions\":[\n  \"Not found in the installed tree and worth a patch-capable specialist: a GDN-specific (delta-rule) analogue of CacheConfig.use_replayssm. ReplaySSM's ring-buffer trick exists only for Mamba2 SSM state; porting the 'cache recent inputs, defer the full-state store' idea to the GDN recurrence would attack the same ~75MB/req/step traffic that bf16 only halves, i.e. a 2-4x further reduction instead of 2x.\",\n  \"Is there an env-only carve-out for the CDNA2 AITER gate? Answer from this tree: no - is_aiter_found_and_supported() (vllm/_aiter_ops.py:134-155) returns get_cdna_version() > 2 with no override; VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 is already set in the base env and does not bypass the arch test.\",\n  \"Which of the 360 prompts actually hit the 38-76% prefix-cache share? If the random-token corpus is reusing prompt prefixes, prefill is cheaper than the 5x38.5s accounting implies and the decode side deserves the remaining slots.\",\n  \"If bf16 state passes throughput but fails the tightened accuracy floor, does --mamba-cache-dtype bfloat16 (conv state only, leaving SSM fp32 via 'auto') recover part of the page-size gain at much lower numerical risk? Not proposed this round because conv state is already bf16-sized by model dtype.\"],\n \"summary\":\"pr_monitor down, so I surveyed the installed 0.28.0+rocm723 tree directly. Answered the round's residual question: the GDN Triton/FLA decode path whitelists bfloat16 recurrent state (FUSED_GDN_STATE_DTYPES=(fp32,bf16)), and --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype overrides the checkpoint's fp32 declaration with only a warning - so bf16 state is benchable as a pure CLI flag. Ruled out as already-present or inapplicable: async scheduling (default-on, and 'align' mode is explicitly patched for it), the CUDA fused GDN decode op (not built), mamba stochastic rounding (CUDA-only), ReplaySSM (Mamba2-only), and AITER's CDNA2 gate (no env override). 3 ranked variants: bf16 state, bf16+TRITON_ATTN, TRITON_ATTN alone.\"}}\nos.makedirs(D,exist_ok=True)\nfor f in (\"specialist_done.partial.json\",):\n    p=os.path.join(D,f+\".tmp\"); json.dump(payload,open(p,\"w\"),indent=1); os.replace(p,os.path.join(D,f))\nprint(\"wrote partial\", len(json.dumps(payload)))\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/hlx/p.py","description":"Write checkpoint partial with findings and 3 proposals"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adf273e6-8b7e-4711-b83b-3db97c0a8d5d","uuid":"c418aa58-0860-48c4-aafb-d6ed2819bac6"}
