{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_92414d208adef48a","type":"tool_result","content":"TITLE: [Bugfix] Reject incompatible mamba_ssm_cache_dtype before it crashes EngineCore\nSTATE: open merged: False base: main\nHEAD_SHA: 23ae4da3cdc84c430963a93b930f6f5bb8246872\nDIFF_URL: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54123.diff\nMERGEABLE: unstable changed_files: 2\nBODY: [Bugfix] Reject incompatible mamba_ssm_cache_dtype before it crashes EngineCore\n\nThe Mamba1 selective_scan CUDA kernel (csrc/libtorch_stable/mamba/ selective_scan_fwd.cu) only supports an SSM state dtype that is either float32 or exactly equal to the model's activation dtype -- its dispatch macro instantiates state_t from ssm_states.scalar_type() while u (the activation input) drives input_t, and the kernel asserts state_type == input_type || state_type == float32 before it will run.\n\nMambaStateDtypeCalculator.mamba1_state_dtype() resolved mamba_ssm_cache_dtype independently of the model's compute dtype whenever it was set to an explicit value, so a config like --dtype float16 --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 passed straight through config validation and model loading, and only failed once the first request hit selective_scan_fwd inside EngineCore, killing the engine with a bare STD_TORCH_CHECK failure at line 791.\n\nValidate the combination in mamba1_state_dtype() itself, where both the model's activation dtype and the requested cache dtype are already available, and raise a clear ValueError naming the incompatible dtypes and how to fix the config. This runs during KV-cache-spec construction at engine init, well before any request reaches EngineCore.\n\nMamba2 and GatedDeltaNet layers never call selective_scan_fn -- they use mamba_chunk_scan_combined_varlen / selective_state_update instead, which don't share this constraint -- so the check is scoped to mamba1_state_dtype() only and mamba2_state_dtype()/gated_delta_net_state_dtype() are left untouched.\n\nFixes #53239\n\n## Purpose\n\n`mamba_ssm_cache_dtype` currently accepts a dtype independent of the model's activation dtype, but the Mamba1 `selective_scan_fwd` CUDA kernel only supports an SSM state dtype that is `float32` or exactly equal to the model's activation dtype. Any other explicit combination passes config validation and model loading today, then crashes EngineCore on the very first request with `RuntimeError: selective_scan_fwd, .../selective_scan_fwd.cu:791`.\n\nThis PR moves that validation into `MambaStateDtypeCalculator.mamba1_state_dtype()`, so the incompatible combination is rejected with a clear `ValueE","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adf273e6-8b7e-4711-b83b-3db97c0a8d5d","uuid":"5d00ae62-7835-4960-bc1e-9f46a981abf4","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:44:59.806Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TITLE: [Bugfix] Reject incompatible mamba_ssm_cache_dtype before it crashes EngineCore\nSTATE: open merged: False base: main\nHEAD_SHA: 23ae4da3cdc84c430963a93b930f6f5bb8246872\nDIFF_URL: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54123.diff\nMERGEABLE: unstable changed_files: 2\nBODY: [Bugfix] Reject incompatible mamba_ssm_cache_dtype before it crashes EngineCore\n\nThe Mamba1 selective_scan CUDA kernel (csrc/libtorch_stable/mamba/ selective_scan_fwd.cu) only supports an SSM state dtype that is either float32 or exactly equal to the model's activation dtype -- its dispatch macro instantiates state_t from ssm_states.scalar_type() while u (the activation input) drives input_t, and the kernel asserts state_type == input_type || state_type == float32 before it will run.\n\nMambaStateDtypeCalculator.mamba1_state_dtype() resolved mamba_ssm_cache_dtype independently of the model's compute dtype whenever it was set to an explicit value, so a config like --dtype float16 --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 passed straight through config validation and model loading, and only failed once the first request hit selective_scan_fwd inside EngineCore, killing the engine with a bare STD_TORCH_CHECK failure at line 791.\n\nValidate the combination in mamba1_state_dtype() itself, where both the model's activation dtype and the requested cache dtype are already available, and raise a clear ValueError naming the incompatible dtypes and how to fix the config. This runs during KV-cache-spec construction at engine init, well before any request reaches EngineCore.\n\nMamba2 and GatedDeltaNet layers never call selective_scan_fn -- they use mamba_chunk_scan_combined_varlen / selective_state_update instead, which don't share this constraint -- so the check is scoped to mamba1_state_dtype() only and mamba2_state_dtype()/gated_delta_net_state_dtype() are left untouched.\n\nFixes #53239\n\n## Purpose\n\n`mamba_ssm_cache_dtype` currently accepts a dtype independent of the model's activation dtype, but the Mamba1 `selective_scan_fwd` CUDA kernel only supports an SSM state dtype that is `float32` or exactly equal to the model's activation dtype. Any other explicit combination passes config validation and model loading today, then crashes EngineCore on the very first request with `RuntimeError: selective_scan_fwd, .../selective_scan_fwd.cu:791`.\n\nThis PR moves that validation into `MambaStateDtypeCalculator.mamba1_state_dtype()`, so the incompatible combination is rejected with a clear `ValueE","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
